  "title": "eax: ensure worksize is at least 16 bytes to prevent buffer underflow",
  "description": "Summary: \n\nIn wsutil/eax.c:dCMAC(), when SizeT is 0 (e.g. empty cleartext and ciphertext), WS_ROUNDUP_16(SizeT) evaluates to 0. In GLib, g_malloc(0) returns a non-NULL pointer, so work == NULL evaluates to false. Subsequently, worksize != SizeT (0 != 0) is false, jumping to the unpadded else branch where ptr = &work\\[worksize - 0x10\\].\n\nBecause worksize is 0, ptr evaluates to &work\\[-16\\], causing BLK_XOR() to write 16 bytes before the allocated heap block (heap buffer underflow / out-of-bounds write, CWE-787).\n\nChanges:\n\n- Ensure worksize is set to at least EAX_SIZEOF_KEY (16 bytes) when SizeT is 0 so standard RFC 4493 CMAC padding (0x80 followed by 15 zeros) is applied and XORed with instance-\\>Q without out-of-bounds access.\n- Guard against integer overflow in WS_ROUNDUP_16.",
  "state": "closed",
