        },
        {
          "id": 3825001687,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "You are right. I confused standard malloc(0) with GLib's g_malloc(0).\n\nSince g_malloc(0) returns NULL, the existing \\`if (work == NULL)\\` check already returns false safely, and the out-of-bounds access never happens.\n\nI will close this MR.",
