      "title": "eax: ensure worksize is at least 16 bytes to prevent buffer underflow",
      "message": "eax: ensure worksize is at least 16 bytes to prevent buffer underflow\n\nIn dCMAC(), when SizeT is 0 (e.g. empty cleartext and ciphertext), WS_ROUNDUP_16(SizeT) evaluates to 0. In GLib, g_malloc(0) returns a non-NULL pointer, causing the check work == NULL to evaluate to false. Subsequently, worksize != SizeT (0 != 0) evaluates to false, jumping to the unpadded branch where ptr = &work[worksize - 0x10].\n\nBecause worksize is 0, ptr evaluates to &work[-16], causing BLK_XOR() to write 16 bytes before the allocated heap block (heap buffer underflow / out-of-bounds write).\n\nEnsure worksize is set to EAX_SIZEOF_KEY (16 bytes) when SizeT is 0 so standard CMAC padding (0x80 followed by zeros) is applied cleanly, and check for overflow in WS_ROUNDUP_16.\n",
      "author_name": "Ayush Meel",
